##### Analysis

{#- Rates are over what was measured, matching how the backend already
    computes `overall_score`. Dividing by every row instead reports a model
    that answered 4 of 4 correctly as 40% when 6 rows could not be read. -#}
{% set total_cases = bench.detailed_results | length %}
{% set total_unmeasured = bench.detailed_results | selectattr('status', 'defined') | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'errored') | list | length %}
{% set total_scored = total_cases - total_unmeasured %}
{#- Counted over scored rows, not all rows. Equivalent today, since an
    errored row always carries `success: False`, but relying on that would
    make `failed` go negative the day one does not. -#}
{% set total_passed = bench.detailed_results | rejectattr('status', 'defined') | selectattr('success') | list | length + (bench.detailed_results | selectattr('status', 'defined') | rejectattr('status', 'equalto', 'errored') | selectattr('success') | list | length) %}
{% set total_failed = total_scored - total_passed %}
{% set pass_rate = total_passed / total_scored if total_scored > 0 else 0 %}

- **Total Test Cases:** {{ total_cases }}
{% if total_scored > 0 %}
- **Passed:** {{ total_passed }} ({{ pass_rate | format_percent }} of {{ total_scored }} measured)
- **Failed:** {{ total_failed }} ({{ (1 - pass_rate) | format_percent }} of {{ total_scored }} measured)
{% else %}
- **Passed / Failed:** not measured, no row could be scored
{% endif %}
{% if total_unmeasured %}
- **Not measured:** {{ total_unmeasured }}
{% endif %}

**Performance by Evaluation Type:**

{% for eval_type, type_results in results_by_type.items() %}
{% set type_unmeasured = type_results | selectattr('status', 'defined') | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'errored') | list | length %}
{% set type_total = type_results | length %}
{% set type_scored = type_total - type_unmeasured %}
{% set type_passed = type_results | rejectattr('status', 'defined') | selectattr('success') | list | length + (type_results | selectattr('status', 'defined') | rejectattr('status', 'equalto', 'errored') | selectattr('success') | list | length) %}
{% if type_scored > 0 %}
{% set type_rate = type_passed / type_scored %}
{% set type_status = "✅" if type_rate >= 0.8 else "⚠️" if type_rate >= 0.5 else "❌" %}
- {{ eval_type | replace('_', ' ') | title }}: {{ type_status }} {{ type_passed }}/{{ type_scored }} ({{ type_rate | format_percent }}){% if type_unmeasured %}, {{ type_unmeasured }} not measured{% endif %}
{% else %}
- {{ eval_type | replace('_', ' ') | title }}: ⚠️ not measured ({{ type_total }} case{{ 's' if type_total != 1 }})
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if total_failed > 0 %}
**Common Failure Patterns:**

{# Failure patterns are about how the MODEL failed, so a row nobody could
   score does not belong here: "row has no expected answer" is a defect in
   the dataset, not a pattern in the answers. Those rows are counted under
   "Not measured" above and detailed in their own block. #}
{% set failure_reasons = {} %}
{% for detail in bench.detailed_results %}
{% if not detail.success and not (detail.status is defined and detail.status == 'errored') %}
{% set reason_key = (detail.reason | default('Unknown')).split('.')[0] %}
{% set _ = failure_reasons.update({reason_key: failure_reasons.get(reason_key, 0) + 1}) %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% for reason, count in failure_reasons | dictsort(by='value', reverse=true) %}
{% if loop.index <= 5 %}
- {{ reason }}: {{ count }} case(s)
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}

